A||||17||fierojp||Need more help with Quad 4 - hot exhaust continues?||||11||
Z||000000||fierojp||11-18-2001||02:38 PM||||Hi,<BR>Got an exhaust put on my quad4 fiero yesterday.  I drove it for a few minutes this morning and everything ran pretty well, but near the end of my drive some smoke began coming from the exhaust (not out of the end but off of the exhaust itself).  Then when I turned it off, smoke continued to rise for a couple of minutes (nothing major, but enough to see easily).  I didn't see any part of the exhaust as being red hot, but it was daytime.  <P>So my question is... is the smoke from the new cat and new custom exhaust (being that it was the first time it had been heated up) or do I still have the same hot exhaust problem I had before I installed the new exhaust (my manifold would get red hot, but I figured it was due to a very rich condition since the exhaust was not complete - O2 sensor picking up outside air). <P>Any help on this one would be greatly appreciated.  Thanks!||||reg||11
Z||000001||koolgtz||11-18-2001||03:32 PM||||As someone who has a Beretta Quad4 for years, I've experienced a lot of problems and what your describing is the new exhaust burning of the oils/grease that on pipes. Once I had a bad oxygen sensor and the cast iron manifold didn't glow red but a lot black smoke came out exhaust and a poor driving condition. ||||reg||7
Z||000002||fierojp||11-18-2001||03:58 PM||||KoolGTZ - Thanks for replying!  Yeah, I'm almost positive you're right.  It's just scary after seeing the red hot manifolds before I had the exhaust installed, and now the smoke...  I think tonight I'll try driving it again so I can check for a glowing condition that could point to other problems.<P>Any one else agree?  Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierojp||11-18-2001||08:06 PM||||Well, I just got done driving it for about three minutes.  The exhaust was glowing red hot all the way past the cat.  AHHHHHHH!  I hope I didn't melt my brand new cat.  I don't have the money to buy another!  <P>So I guess I'm still running lean or rich, but I don't know which.  The oxygen sensor reports no codes.  <P>Where should I start now?  Please reply!  I need help!||||reg||9
Z||000004||fierojp||11-18-2001||10:37 PM||||Anyone???  PLEEAAAZZZEE!||||reg||1
Z||000005||koolgtz||11-19-2001||08:47 PM||||That's strange. If the oxygen sensor isn't giving a code then its not lean or rich. Is it possible that due to the confine space in the rear of the fiero excessive heat is being retained in the pipe making it glow. Remember the V6 manifolds glow also. I spent a lot of time at <A HREF="http://groups.yahoo.com/group/quadfourm" TARGET=_blank>http://groups.yahoo.com/group/quadfourm</A>  Go there and see if someone can offer some more information. When I'm finish with my Q4 Fiero I got to watch for that same problem that your having.||||reg||1
Z||000006||fierojp||11-20-2001||09:47 AM||||KoolGTZ - Yeah I have no idea what's going on.  The exhaust, though, was red hot glowing brightly - definitely not normal. It was a new oxygen sensor.  Can they be ruined by excessive heat in a way that they would not send any codes???<P>Thanks for the quadforum link.  I'll see if they can help... ||||reg||1
Z||000007||koolgtz||11-20-2001||05:13 PM||||Are you using the stock cast iron exhaust Q4 HO manifold? If you are then that's alot heat to make cast iron glow. The other Q4 is made of mild steel and that can glow very easy. Do you have any type of vaccum leaks?||||reg||1
Z||000008||fierojp||11-20-2001||06:27 PM||||I think... I hope I have it figured out.  The quadfourm on Yahoo said that it could be a problem with the computer I'm using with the '88 engine.  It's a remanu. ECM that might not be an '88.  Apparently this would definitely cause a timing problem...  I'm trying to get in touch with Boomtastic (the guy I bought the engine and ECM from) to verify the years.  It sounds like if it's an '88, I would have to find an '88 ECM and then get a custom PROM burned.  Sucks, cuz I'm outta money after this rather costly conversion thus far...<P>Thanks,<BR>JP||||reg||1
Z||000009||Standard||11-20-2001||09:52 PM||||I've seen my exhaust manifold glow slightly after some hard running when it was actually warm up here, but never the entire exhaust...<P>Got any pics of how you ran your exhaust?<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">          <BR><FONT COLOR="red">1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed</FONT><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="white">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000010||koolgtz||11-20-2001||11:01 PM||||Fierojp, I read your post on the quadforum and I must tell you those guys live and breath quad4's as you could see. If you have any more problems post it there. About the chip try http//www. mantapart.com the deal with GM small FWD cars.They might do some custom work. The guy's on the forum will offer more places to try.||||reg||6
Z||000011||fierojp||11-20-2001||11:32 PM||||I don't have any pics... yet.  I'll try to get some soon if you're interested.  It's a very basic exhaust.  Comes out of the manifold, down and towards the passenger side of the trunk.  Then curves back toward the driver's side and into the cat.  Then farther left until lined up with the exhaust cutout in the rear bumper.  No muffler.  Wish I would've had a camera to capture the glowing red hot condition!<P>The guy I bought the engine from isn't sure what year it was.  He thinks it was an '89.  I think it's probably an '88 though - so I need to check that out.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Standard||11-21-2001||02:01 AM||||How does it sound with no muffler?  My setup starts like yours, but after the cat it curves back around to the pass. side so a stock Fiero muffler can be used.  Right now I have a straight pipe going into a single in/dual out muffler.  Sounds a bit 'ricey' from 2000-3500 rpm, then just screams after that.  Sounded a bit throatier when I had a hollow cat on there.  I'm trying to decide if I want to get rid of the cat totally and go straight to the muffler, or do a setup like yours.<P>My setup when new..<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/quad_exhaust_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||fierojp||11-21-2001||10:04 AM||||standard - I see you cut your trunk out.  I didn't.  That's why I can't fit the muffler.  I just drove it for a few minutes and not at high RPM's, but I didn't sound too obnoxious.  I will probably add a resonator tip of somekind.  Might take off another decibel or two.<P>JP||||reg||1
